SLUG: services/office-relocation.html
TITLE: Office Relocation in Kanpur — commercial moving
DESC: Office and commercial relocation in Kanpur planned around your downtime: desks numbered to a new floor plan, IT reconnected, records in sealed crates, weekend slots.
HEADING: Office &amp; commercial relocation
LEAD: Planned around your downtime rather than ours. The goal is simple: staff come back to a working office, not a room full of boxes.
CRUMBS: Home|/ ; Services|/services.html ; Office relocation|
---

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split is-wide-left">
        <div>
          <h2>An office move is a scheduling job</h2>
          <p class="lead">
            Moving a house is about care. Moving an office is about sequence.
            The furniture is the easy part — what decides whether Monday goes
            well is whether every desk, cable and file ends up where the floor
            plan says it should.
          </p>
          <p>
            We start from your new floor plan. Every desk and cabinet is
            numbered and mapped to its destination position before anything is
            lifted, so the crew is placing items, not guessing. Records move in
            sealed, numbered crates rather than open cartons, and IT is handled
            as its own sequence with its own checklist.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <span class="card__icon"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-building"/></svg></span>
          <h3>Included as standard</h3>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Pre-move survey of both floors, with a written sequence plan</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Desks and cabinets numbered against the new floor plan</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Workstations dismantled and rebuilt in position</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Documents in sealed, numbered crates with a chain-of-custody list</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Monitors, CPUs and peripherals bagged per desk, not pooled</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Weekend, evening and overnight slots</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-sunk">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Planning</span>
        <h2>What we need from you, and when</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Office moves go wrong in the planning, not on the day. These are the
          decisions that need to be made before the date is fixed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Three weeks out</h3>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Confirm the new floor plan and desk numbering</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Book building access and service lifts at both ends</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Name one decision-maker for move day</span></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>One week out</h3>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Staff clear personal items and label their own crate</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>IT confirms what is being disconnected, and by whom</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Confidential files identified and crated separately</span></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Move day</h3>
          <ul class="ticks">
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Your decision-maker on site at both addresses</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Crate list checked and signed at both ends</span></li>
            <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Priority desks rebuilt first so key staff can start</span></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>What changes the price</h2>
          <ol class="steps mt-6">
            <li class="step"><div>
              <h3>Headcount and workstation count</h3>
              <p>The practical unit of an office move is the desk, not the square foot.</p>
            </div></li>
            <li class="step"><div>
              <h3>How much IT we handle</h3>
              <p>Bagging and moving equipment is routine. Disconnecting and recommissioning servers and network hardware is specialist work and is priced separately.</p>
            </div></li>
            <li class="step"><div>
              <h3>Lift and loading access</h3>
              <p>A service lift booked for exclusive use transforms the timeline. Sharing a passenger lift with a working building does the opposite.</p>
            </div></li>
            <li class="step"><div>
              <h3>The window</h3>
              <p>A full weekend is the cheapest way to do it. Compressing the same work into one night costs more because it needs a larger crew.</p>
            </div></li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2>Questions we get asked</h2>
          <div class="faq mt-6" data-faq>
            <details>
              <summary>Can you move us over a weekend so we do not lose a working day?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                Yes, and for most offices that is the right choice. Two clear
                days lets us move, rebuild and have IT reconnected before staff
                return. Weekend slots book out earliest, so fix the date well
                in advance.
              </p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Do you handle the servers and network equipment?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                We move the hardware safely, and we coordinate around your IT
                team's schedule. We do not present ourselves as network
                engineers: disconnection, racking and recommissioning should be
                done by whoever supports your infrastructure, and we plan the
                move sequence around them.
              </p></div>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>How do you protect confidential files?</summary>
              <div class="faq__body"><p>
                They go into sealed, numbered crates listed on their own
                manifest, signed out at the old office and signed in at the
                new one. If you need a specific chain-of-custody procedure,
                tell us at survey and we will work to it.
              </p></div>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- Photographs of real jobs. Generated by
       tools/gallery/add-photo-strips.ps1 -- edit the mapping there, not
       here, or the next run will not know this strip exists. -->
  <section class="section is-tight on-sunk" aria-labelledby="shots-service-office-relocation" data-photo-strip>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">From our own jobs</span>
        <h2 id="shots-service-office-relocation">Records and equipment, crated and strapped</h2>
        <p class="lead">Boxed records strapped into stacks and moved on a trolley, and trunks finished with edge protection.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="workshots">
        <figure class="workshot">
          <img class="workshot__img"
               src="/assets/images/gallery/strapped-cartons-on-trolley-400.jpg"
